Using \(\cos x=\frac1{\sqrt5}\) and \(\sin x=-\frac2{\sqrt5}\),

\[
\frac{2\cos^2\frac x2-\sin x-1}{\sin x+\cos x}
=
\frac{\cos x-\sin x}{\sin x+\cos x}
=
\frac{\frac1{\sqrt5}-\left(-\frac2{\sqrt5}\right)}{-\frac2{\sqrt5}+\frac1{\sqrt5}}
=
\frac{\frac3{\sqrt5}}{-\frac1{\sqrt5}}
=-3.
\]

\[
\boxed{-3}
\]
